WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.520
All right, let's get into audience questions&nbsp;
for the week, David. Shouldn't Joe Biden be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:08.160
bragging about the stock market the way Trump&nbsp;
did? I don't mean because Joe Biden is actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:13.200
responsible for the stock market, but because&nbsp;
Trump seemed to do well when he bragged about it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.880
I like the way that this question is asked because&nbsp;
it's not being asked as a question of whether Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:25.680
Biden deserves credit. I mean, as we've talked&nbsp;
about before, to some degree, the sort of economic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.680 --> 00:00:32.320
circumstances over which a president has&nbsp;
some influence impact the stock market.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:38.880
But the stock market performance alone is often&nbsp;
used kind of as a political football. And Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:43.360
Trump certainly regularly would talk about how&nbsp;
great the stock market is doing when it was up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:48.560
not when it was down and many of his followers&nbsp;
fell for it. It's really a question of whether&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:54.000
politically it would be advantageous for Joe Biden&nbsp;
to do it. I think that it's not clear that it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:01.040
would because Joe Biden's base is so different&nbsp;
than Donald Trump's base. Donald Trump's base&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:07.360
was disproportionately made up of people who were&nbsp;
never involved in politics before or who were, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:13.440
they fell for Republican nonsense. So they were&nbsp;
like the perfect marks for just hearing from Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:21.120
about the stock market. And the Joe Biden base is&nbsp;
different. And it doesn't strike me as something&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:28.000
that would be so obviously beneficial for Joe&nbsp;
Biden to brag about the stock market in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:33.760
same way that Donald Trump did. Now, that being&nbsp;
said, just because you don't have the sort of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:39.280
sycophantic cult of personality cheerleaders on&nbsp;
the left that you had on the right around Donald&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.280 --> 00:01:45.440
Trump doesn't mean Joe Biden shouldn't talk about&nbsp;
the stock market in the context of talking about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:51.760
how we're doing. So certainly Joe Biden should be&nbsp;
saying we're vaccinating more than three million&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:59.600
a day. Covid deaths are down 77 percent. Cases are&nbsp;
down roughly the same percentage. Unemployment is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:05.520
down. We are seeing job creation. Stock market&nbsp;
is at record highs on and. So it's a package&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:12.480
overall. But if the question is, should Joe Biden&nbsp;
start tweeting about the stock market from a golf&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:17.360
course, the way, you know, the caricature of&nbsp;
what Donald Trump was doing, I don't think it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:23.680
it's what Joe Biden should be doing. One other&nbsp;
aspect to why it's important for Biden to talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:33.600
about the stock market numbers is that you&nbsp;
do want to try at least to get the media to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:40.400
put out messages that are advantageous to&nbsp;
you. Any president would try to do this. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:46.080
rather than just leaving it to corporate media&nbsp;
to figure out, oh, the stock market is doing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:50.720
well. And Joe Biden's president and we were told&nbsp;
that it was going to be a disaster by Trump if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:56.000
Joe Biden were president, why not? Again,&nbsp;
this is sort of like communications and PR&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.800 --> 00:03:02.480
feed the story to the media in, in some&nbsp;
sense, what one other aspect of this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:10.240
When Donald Trump insisted during the campaign&nbsp;
that if Joe Biden wins, your 401. KS will be worth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:16.800
nothing, the economy will collapse, unemployment&nbsp;
will explode, covid death will explode, suicides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.960
will explode, you won't have windows in buildings,&nbsp;
you won't have indoor heating, you won't have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:24.880
indoor cooling. You'll have to flush the toilet&nbsp;
10 to 15 times. You'll have to run your dishwasher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:30.880
two or three times to get your dishes cleaned. We&nbsp;
knew all that stuff was crazy, but in particular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:39.440
now Joe Biden talking about what the stock market&nbsp;
is doing might be a good way to get media outlets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:46.000
to put more Republicans on the spot and say you&nbsp;
agreed with Trump during the campaign that if Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:49.600
Biden were president, this would happen to the&nbsp;
market. The markets are at record highs. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:55.200
say you? They would almost certainly retreat to&nbsp;
something like, well, Joe Biden has inflated the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:00.720
stock market by, quote, printing money through&nbsp;
stimulus. And he wants to do infrastructure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:06.720
but they'll be on the ropes and they will have a&nbsp;
defense. It'll be a really stupid defense. So the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:15.520
position Joe Biden should take is take credit&nbsp;
for turning things around and talk about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.520 --> 00:04:21.360
stock market as one of many indicators as&nbsp;
to how things are continuing to improve.

